lines=['# Expanded Kalshi perpetual research — September 26, 2026','','## Decision','','There are concrete candidates for forward paper testing: LTC aligned 24h/72h trend first; BCH only as the aggressive comparator; ETH as a long-only benchmark rather than a priority bot after control testing. This is a research ranking, not a live-allocation recommendation. Keep gold reversal as an existing comparator. Do not run every strategy with $50 simultaneously: the research allocation cap is $50 aggregate for a $100 portfolio, and these isolated backtests are not additive.','','Fresh census still has 25 products. Four additional rules per product plus five economically chosen paired strategies and two cross-sectional strategies produced 107 strategy/product families and 538 clock variants. Every variant is retained. Three products (DOT/HBAR/XLM) have no returned candles, and newly listed metals can have too little continuous data to produce signals. Zero trades means insufficient data/no trigger, not a tested profitable or unprofitable strategy.','','## What the shortlist would trade','','Aligned trend: go long only when both the preceding 24-hour and 72-hour midpoint returns are positive; short only when both are negative; otherwise remain flat. Hold24hours. Require72 continuous hours of quotes, current completed-hour volume >0 and signal spread <=20bp. Test four fixed UTC schedules (00/06/12/18), with entry and exit each delayed one hour. All current taker fees, observed funding, bid/ask crossing and extra execution costs are charged. Maximum$50 notional, whole contracts; no leveraged return multiplier. This is lower frequency than the existing 15-minute prediction bot.','','| Candidate | Median schedule P&L | Extra5bp each leg | Profitable schedules | Median recent14d | Worst observed hourly drawdown | Trades/schedule |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
